  dishName: Adobo
  dishSprite: {fileID: -2905549093005077656, guid: 41524c236021f9f4894cf6d21896aba9, type: 3}
  pages:
  - Great work. The pot in front of you carries a technique our ancestors mastered
    before refrigeration ever reached these shores.
  - "Every family who ever made adobo stretched a day\u2019s catch into a week\u2019s
    meals using nothing more complicated than vinegar and patience."
  - "The next time someone calls adobo \u201Cjust\u201D a Filipino dish, you can
    tell them it \r\nis also a thousand-year-old survival strategy,"
  - "a cultural bridge between pre-colonial Austronesia and colonial Spain, and a
    quiet reminder that the oldest kitchen tools we have are time and acid.\r"
